son compares the weighted maximum magnitude and prefers the one with the lower value, because a lower value means less severe potential loss. Thus, A: 3000 × 1 = 3000, B: 4000 × 0.8 = 3200. Since 3000 < 3200, A has a lower weighted maximum magnitude and is preferred. Therefore, the reason would prefer A. So the reason can be applied to the decision problem, and it leads to preferring A.",
